{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_session_86_combined_handoff", "label": "Session 86 Combined Handoff", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-86-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_session_86_combined_gauss_cut", "label": "The Gauss Cut: K = 1 Is Sharp Over the Gauss-Admissible Set", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-86-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The saturating tent is Gauss-admissible at 74/74 channels and the two constraints exclude nothing at the 50 channels with K >= 1 - the admissible set and the K >= 1 set are identical, so Gauss bites only where the bound already certifies. The falsification of S6 IS the set identity."}, {"id": "recovered_session_86_combined_h1_finite_kinetic_energy", "label": "The Excluding Constraint Is H^1, Not Gauss", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-86-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A saturating kink means a discontinuous orbital and infinite kinetic energy, so the constraint that can exclude it belongs to the Schroedinger equation's language rather than Gauss's. Nothing else in the q-language can move the threshold."}, {"id": "recovered_session_86_combined_f86_1", "label": "F86.1 S4 Scorer Used the Wrong Statistic", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-86-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_session_86_combined_f86_2", "label": "F86.2 Lever Sited Where the Dead Arm Has No Region", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/SESSION-86-COMBINED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}